        Many users wonder how a <strong>copy and paste font</strong> tool changes lettering styles across apps like Instagram, TikTok, Discord, and WhatsApp without requiring custom font files. The secret lies in universal Unicode standards.
      </p>
      <p>
        Traditional font files (.ttf or .otf) change how an operating system draws letter glyphs locally on your screen. When posting on social platforms, however, you cannot embed font files into a bio. Instead, our <strong>fancy fonts</strong> engine uses Unicode Mathematical Alphanumeric Symbols from the Supplementary Multilingual Plane.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you use our tool, you are converting standard characters into authentic Unicode symbols representing cursive script, gothic blackletter, or double-struck letters. Because modern operating systems natively support these symbols, your decorative text displays reliably across iPhones, Android devices, Mac, and Windows.
      </p>
